      "title": "The federal holidays \"within the District of Columbia\" of 37 C.F.R.\n§§ 1.7(a) and 2.196: the legal public holidays of 5 U.S.C. § 6103(a), observed under\n§ 6103(b)(1), plus Inauguration Day, which § 6103(c) makes a holiday for\nfederal employees in the District of Columbia area. Unlike the other\nholidays, § 6103(c) moves only a Sunday Inauguration Day (to Monday); a\nSaturday one is not observed on Friday (unlike core's\n`rcfc-legal-holidays`, which observes it then). Effective dates are those\nof core's `us-federal-holidays`.",
